   174	## 3. An all-family S4 criterion via V4 and Fox colorings
   175	
   176	The direct six-color search is unnecessary.  Let `V4` be the normal Klein
   177	four subgroup of `S4`.  The action on the three partitions of four letters
   178	into two unordered pairs gives
   179	
   180	```text
   181	1 -> V4 -> S4 -> S3 -> 1.                              (3.1)
   182	```
   183	
   184	Each of the six transpositions of `S4` maps to a transposition of `S3`, and
   185	each `S3` transposition has exactly two transposition lifts.  Therefore the
   186	quotient of an `S4` transposition coloring is an ordinary Fox 3-coloring.
   187	For a closed `n`-braid the quotient fixed-point equations are linear over
   188	`F3`; the replay computes their nullspace exactly.
   189	
   190	Fix a nonconstant Fox coloring `rho`.  It is onto `S3`.  Choosing one of the
   191	two transposition lifts at each braid meridian gives `n` bits.  Conjugation of
   192	transpositions in each fixed quotient-color pair is affine in those bits, so
   193	the braid closure equations define an affine `F2` solution space `L_rho`.
   194	
   195	There are exactly four non-full lifts in `L_rho`: composing `rho` with the
   196	four sections `S3 -> S4` whose images are the four point stabilizers.  Conversely,
   197	any lift image projects onto `S3`.  Its intersection with `V4` is invariant
   198	under `S3`; since `S3` acts transitively on the three nonidentity elements of
   199	`V4`, that intersection is either trivial or all of `V4`.  The former case is
   200	one of the four complements, and the latter case is all of `S4`.  Hence
   201	
   202	```text
   203	number of labelled full-S4 colorings
   204	  = sum over nonconstant rho of (|L_rho|-4),            (3.2)
   205	
   206	full S4 exists iff dim_F2(L_rho) >= 3 for some rho.     (3.3)
   207	```
   208	
   209	Equations (3.2)--(3.3) are an exact all-knot-family criterion, not a heuristic
   210	pattern in the first few conductors.  They reduce the old `6^(n-1)` search to
   211	linear algebra over `F3` and `F2`.  The replay independently constructs the
   212	actual `S4` lifts and compares their generated subgroups with all 24 elements
   213	on every tiny row of at most four strands.  Those labelled counts equal the
   214	old direct Hurwitz enumeration exactly.  A deliberate mutation of the affine
   215	lift table fails this complement/lift gate.
