   236	There is also a degree-independent group floor: transposition generators of a
   237	transitive subgroup of `S_d` form a connected graph on `d` vertices, hence
   238	require at least `d-1` distinct edges.  In degree four this forces meridional
   239	rank, and therefore bridge number, at least three.  This explains every
   240	two-bridge kill without enumeration.  Formula (4.2) is the next reusable
